.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap14/review_pass1_supported.log:3754:./.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:640:- algorithm summary: `stmap13` keeps the classic `map` SCL genlib gain default of `250` and passes `fSkipFanout = 14` into the mapper. `mapperMatch.c` treats mode `14` as the same decision policy as `stmap12` mode `13`: delay matching and small-graph/area-flow behavior match the existing shape-gated fanout guard, and exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the tight-depth one-to-two inverter slack area-relief bypass only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. Mode `14` additionally records exact-area risky-cut, fanout-bucket, middle-slack, relief, and rejection counters; `mapperCore.c` prints one `stmap13 guard stats` line after mapping. Existing `map` and `stmap0` through `stmap12` behavior are preserved because modes `0` through `13` retain their prior meanings.
